**How to implement.** The second half of the run rules the forward model needs: how a slot binds for a run and what the source emits, written today inside `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:chartForRun` (steps 252 and 265) and `model.runEmission` (step 266), MOVE into Domain and the table calls them (001 §N 'One item-model evaluator'; .spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move'; step 251: `boundWith` is 'the door S8.2's slots and S11.2's forward model call'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.2. In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs`, which opens `Setups`, after `ItemModelChoice.boundWith` (step 251): (1) `[<ReferenceEquality>] SlotRunParam = { library : LibraryProxy; materials : MaterialProxy; items : Item list; choiceOf : Item -> ItemModelChoice option; valuesOf : Item -> ParameterValues }`: the library a bare slot is bound in, the material store a stack sample resolves through (`MaterialLibrary.fs:MaterialProxy`), the kit's items, an item's model as the window's stores resolve it (`model.tryItemModelChoice`, step 263) and the numbers an item is evaluated with. (2) `SlotRunError`, an `*Error` union: `SlotItemErr of error : SetupError` | `SlotEvaluationErr of error : ItemEvaluationError`, with `member this.describe : string` answering the inner error's `describe` unchanged. (3) `type SetupSlot with member this.runElementWith (param : SlotRunParam) : Result<BoundOpticalElement option, SlotRunError>`, the binding `chartForRun` does once per path step today, by the slot's `placement.catalogueKind`: a `LightSource`, `Detector`, `Lens`, `FlatMirror` or `CurvedMirror` slot answers `Ok None` (a source emits, a detector reads, and a mirror or a lens only steers the ray, as the run law has always treated them); a `LinearPolarizer`, `CircularPolarizer` or `Sample` slot holding `ItemInSlot (id, _)` takes the item of that id in `param.items`, else `SlotItemErr` of `UnknownSlotItemErr` naming the id, then its `param.choiceOf`, else `SlotItemErr` of `UnknownSlotItemErr` naming the item's label and that its model is not in the library, then `choice.boundWith param.materials (param.valuesOf item)` (step 251), its error as `SlotEvaluationErr`; such a slot of `EmptySlotContent` is its library binding: a polarizer slot bound to a `PolarizerItem p` is `BoundPolarizerPreset p.behavior`, a sample slot bound to a `SampleItem s` is `BoundOpticalElement.ofStackSample param.materials (ParameterValues.defaultsOf s.parameterAxes) s` (step 252), and an unbound slot, any other entry or a binding `library.tryGetEntry` does not answer (`Ok None` or `Error`) is `Ok None`, as today. The reasons are the ones `chartForRun` gives today (steps 263, 265). `member this.runStepOf (mueller : MuellerMatrix) : ExperimentRun.RunStep`: an `ObjectStep` for a `Sample` slot and an `ElementStep` for any other (step 265). `static member runEmissionOf (slots : SetupSlot list) (param : SlotRunParam) : Result<SourceEmission, SlotRunError>`, `model.runEmission`'s rule (step 266): the first `LightSource` slot holding an item emits `choice.emissionWith (param.valuesOf item)` (step 246), the item and its model found as above and an evaluation error answered as `SlotEvaluationErr`; without such a slot, `SourceEmission.ofValues (ParameterValues.defaultsOf SourcePreset.lightSourceAxes)` (step 252's default). (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `chartForRun` binds each path step's slot through `slot.runElementWith` over `{ library = model.library; materials = model.materials; items = model.kitItems; choiceOf = model.tryItemModelChoice; valuesOf = fun item -> ParameterValues.ofParameters item.parameters }` and makes each evaluated matrix its step through `slot.runStepOf`; `model.runEmission` is `SetupSlot.runEmissionOf model.elements` over the same param, its error's `describe` as its `ControlCaption`. The failure charts keep their texts: `SlotEvaluationErr (SampleMaterialErr e)` shows `Sample materials failed to resolve` with `e.runFailureCaption`, every other error `The run cannot be evaluated` with its `describe`. The inline bindings are deleted, so one rule binds a slot, and every chart's numbers and texts are unchanged. Tests, in `ItemEvaluationTests` (step 245), with materials from `BuiltinCatalogue.materialStore (fun _ -> [])` and `BuiltinCatalogue.library ()`, over slots built as `SetupTests`' fixtures build them (step 256) and items made by `ItemDraft` (step 216): `a slot runs as its item through the given values, else as its library binding, and a source, detector, mirror or lens slot is no run element`: a linear-polarizer slot bound to `PresetIds.polarizerLp` with no item binds its `BoundPolarizerPreset`; the same slot holding a real-LP item (`ItemModelIds.realLinearPolarizerModelId`) whose `valuesOf` answers an `extinctionRatio` of 0.01 evaluates at 0° and 600 nm to `BoundOpticalElement.ofOpticalForm` of those values, within 1e-12; a sample slot bound to `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` evaluates as `ofStackSample` at its defaults; a source, a detector and a flat-mirror slot answer `Ok None`; and `runStepOf` makes an `ObjectStep` of the sample slot and an `ElementStep` of the polarizer. `a slot whose item the kit lacks or whose model does not resolve answers SlotItemErr`: a polarizer slot holding an item id outside `items`, and one holding an item whose `choiceOf` answers `None`, each answer `SlotItemErr` of `UnknownSlotItemErr`. `the run's source emits its item's state through the given values, and the default set without a source item`: a source slot holding a HeNe item (`BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.heNe633`) whose `valuesOf` answers a degree of polarization 1 at azimuth 30° emits that `SourceEmission`; slots with no source item emit the default emission; and a `degreeOfPolarization` of 1.5 answers `SlotEvaluationErr` of `ParameterOutOfRangeErr`. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.

**Acceptance.** After the move, `SetupSlot.runElementWith`, `runStepOf` and `runEmissionOf` MUST bind a slot and emit the source in Domain, and `chartForRun` and `model.runEmission` MUST call them with no inline binding left; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a slot runs as its item through the given values, else as its library binding, and a source, detector, mirror or lens slot is no run element`, `a slot whose item the kit lacks or whose model does not resolve answers SlotItemErr` and `the run's source emits its item's state through the given values, and the default set without a source item`, the count rising by 3; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, every chart unchanged and the count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s37 invariants MUST pass.
